{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TjuhgmD8L2i7fLByx9ikdu","type":"tool_result","content":"# ADR-008: Serialized server state and unidirectional hydration\n\n**Date:** 2026-10-04\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n\n## Context\n\nThe hydration example scattered application state across component\nhosts. The counter owned its own count, seeded from an attribute; the\nserver hard-coded the values it rendered; and the browser had no way to\nlearn what state the server rendered from. ADR-007 gives the templater a\nbrowser build and `mount`, so the same page function can run on both\nsides -- but only if both sides start from the same state.\n\nAlternatives considered:\n\n- Read state back out of the rendered DOM (attributes, text). Rejected:\n  it couples state to presentation, and not every value is rendered.\n- A library-level state container or hydration helper. Rejected: out of\n  scope for the library, and it would grow the core bundle (ADR-004).\n- Serialize every signal automatically. Rejected: it hides which data\n  crosses the wire; an explicit serialize function keeps it visible.\n\ndocs/adr/ADR-006-hono-html-scaffold.md\ndocs/adr/ADR-005-single-file-components-with-build-time-render-stripping.md\ndocs/adr/ADR-005-single-file-components-with-build-time-render-stripping.md:67:## Note (2026-10-04)\ndocs/adr/ADR-006-hono-html-scaffold.md:69:## Note (2026-10-04)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2d202f7-a9a8-4a4a-920f-a8056edec66f","uuid":"62fa597e-24f1-4525-8727-79178856b20b","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:11:05.162Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# ADR-008: Serialized server state and unidirectional hydration\n\n**Date:** 2026-10-04\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n\n## Context\n\nThe hydration example scattered application state across component\nhosts. The counter owned its own count, seeded from an attribute; the\nserver hard-coded the values it rendered; and the browser had no way to\nlearn what state the server rendered from. ADR-007 gives the templater a\nbrowser build and `mount`, so the same page function can run on both\nsides -- but only if both sides start from the same state.\n\nAlternatives considered:\n\n- Read state back out of the rendered DOM (attributes, text). Rejected:\n  it couples state to presentation, and not every value is rendered.\n- A library-level state container or hydration helper. Rejected: out of\n  scope for the library, and it would grow the core bundle (ADR-004).\n- Serialize every signal automatically. Rejected: it hides which data\n  crosses the wire; an explicit serialize function keeps it visible.\n\ndocs/adr/ADR-006-hono-html-scaffold.md\ndocs/adr/ADR-005-single-file-components-with-build-time-render-stripping.md\ndocs/adr/ADR-005-single-file-components-with-build-time-render-stripping.md:67:## Note (2026-10-04)\ndocs/adr/ADR-006-hono-html-scaffold.md:69:## Note (2026-10-04)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TjuhgmD8L2i7fLByx9ikdu","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
