{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3NRAZC47bV2Y8kkZyEV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] ADR-008 ends with a dated note attributing the measurements to millitags and its toolchain, giving the three brotli sizes and the recovered fraction, and the deserializer import costs against `JSON.parse`.\n[x] The note states the conclusion and leaves the Decision, Trade-offs and Consequences sections unchanged.\n[x] The note contains no em dashes and no arrow characters.\n\nADR-008 now ends with a dated note holding the millitags measurements, and the full `npm test` run passes, 286 of 286. It's committed as `dbdc080`. The only file changed is `docs/adr/ADR-008-serialized-server-state.md`; `docs/adr/INDEX.md` is untouched.\n\n- **Where the numbers came from:** I didn't open `../millitags` again, because this run's rules don't allow reading outside the worktree. I took the figures from the previous attempt's notes, which copied them from millitags' ADR-005 (\"The narrowed serialization payload\", measured 2026-08-18) and the header of its `src/revive.ts`. They are internally consistent:\n  - **Payload:** 509 B of HTML plus 496 B of JSON comes to 1005 B. Sent together they compress to 967 B, so the compressor recovers 38 B, which is 7.7% of the payload.\n  - **Revivers:** devalue (1959 bytes), turbo-stream (2477) and seroval (3425) are each more than half of millitags' 3519-byte core. \"Core bundle\" means millitags' own core, as its source says.\n- **What the note says:** a table of the three brotli sizes and the recovered fraction, then a table of reviver import costs against `JSON.parse` (32 bytes). It ends with ADR-008's existing conclusion: keep the payload narrow and keep `JSON.parse` as the reviver, citing ADR-004's bundle-size priority. The diff only adds lines, so the Decision, Trade-offs and Consequences sections are as they were. A search for em dash and arrow characters finds none.\n- **Why attempt 1 failed:** another worktree's test run was already using port 8123. The ADR change wasn't the cause. That attempt's commit was also missing from this worktree, which is why I rewrote the note.\n- **Build first in a fresh worktree:** the first `npm test` failed typechecking because `dist/` hadn't been built, as AGENTS.md warns. After `npm run build` it passed.\n\nI wrote no tests, because the global rules say not to test docs, and the lint script only covers `.ts`/`.js` files. AGENTS.md already covers the build-before-test step and the spec already covers the shared port, so I added nothing to AGENTS.md. Notes are in `.nightralph/notes.md` (not committed)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":189,"cache_read_input_tokens":56346,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":189},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2d202f7-a9a8-4a4a-920f-a8056edec66f","uuid":"014cd6f3-dbed-4f7a-9df2-0f0fa0f798b4","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:12:05.605Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3NRADbWxFmZkLrUHi7r"}
